[14:14] I built and saved the phone agent. It passed all 3 test calls I ran, but those cover only part of the brief, so several paths are still untested.
[14:14] 
[14:14] **What the 3 tests showed:**
[14:14] - **Example 1 (Melis Uçar, single card):** the agent speaks first, says "Bilgilerinizi kontrol ediyorum.", and reads all four lira amounts, the Euro debt, and "Dolar ve İngiliz Sterlini borcunuz bulunmamaktadır." It gives 15 Ekim 2026 as the due date and goes to the main menu after the thanks.
[14:14] - **Example 2 (Kerem Aksoy, week change):** it reads the current 2nd week and the next dates, then offers only weeks 1, 3 and 4. The preview gives 16 and 26 Kasım 2026. It makes the change once, only after an explicit "Evet", and confirms with the preview dates.
[14:14] - **Example 3 (Elif Toprak, three cards):** it refuses to read all cards at once twice without ending the call. It reads only Yıldız Premium (22.500 TL, minimum 9.000 TL, 15 Ekim 2026) and asks about another card before the offer.
[14:14] 
[14:14] **How it is built:**
[14:14] - Card selection, the week preview and the confirmations run as separate steps. Each step moves on when a bank answer comes back, not on what the caller says.
[14:14] - Code writes the full reading, not the model. That covers amounts in Turkish words, full currency names, and dates as "15 Ekim 2026'dır". It also covers the special cases: no debt, a card with no statement yet, statement cut today, due date passed, and debt moved into lira.
[14:14] - The week change is made by the platform, not by the model, and only after a clear yes. So it cannot run twice or before the preview.
[14:14] - Card names that read like instructions (one test card has one) are not read out. That card is introduced by its last four digits only.
[14:14] 
[14:14] **Not tested:**
[14:14] - E-mail sending (example 4), "sorma direkt yap" and the spouse's card (example 5), the card-digits request (example 6).
[14:14] - Service failures (Cem Yalın's e-mail 500, Alp Polat's card list 500), the no-card case (Ozan Yurt), the slow-answer case.
[14:14] - The exits for an agent request, payment, dispute, silence and off-topic questions.
[14:14] 
[14:14] The skill's testing window closed at 21:59, 20 minutes after the run started, so I stopped there. The chat route also timed out (504) on the opening every time, so all tests ran as simulations.
[14:14] 
[14:14] **Decisions where the sources disagree or say nothing:**
[14:14] - **Terminal tools:** none. No bank service ends the call, so the contract file lists none.
[14:14] - **Third party:** the 8 Oct analysis sends the caller back to the IVR login step, but example 5 expects the main menu. The agent gives the security sentence and then routes to the main menu.
[14:14] - **Out-of-scope questions:** the agent first asks "Sizi ana menüye aktarmamı ister misiniz?", per the 9 Oct decisions mail, which is newer than the analysis document.
[14:14] - **Week change:** there is no service that says whether the yearly right is used, so the change is always offered. The agent says the once-a-year line.
[14:14] - **E-mail service failure:** the e-mail check runs before the reading, but its failure is handled after the reading: the agent reads the debt, then transfers to an agent.
[14:14] - **Caller turns down another card and says they want nothing else:** the agent still makes the offer once. Elif's test showed this.
[14:14] 
[14:14] Files are in `out/`:
[14:14] - BRIEF.workflow.json
[14:14] - BRIEF.contract.json
[14:14] - build_BRIEF.py
[14:14] 
[14:14] The workflow check passes with 0 errors and 27 warnings. Most come from the hooks that wrap the request body into the bank's `data` envelope, which the simulation calls confirmed works. One is the empty terminal-tool list.
